id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDY2Mjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1106629?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux","html_url":"https://github.com/zeux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-28T16:19:23Z","updated_at":"2025-08-28T16:19:23Z","body":"No, import time should be the same with or without this flag.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3234145970/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3235113001","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110028#issuecomment-3235113001","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110028","id":3235113001,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7A0-gp","user":{"login":"zeux","id":1106629,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMDY2Mjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1106629?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux","html_url":"https://github.com/zeux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zeux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-28T22:16:32Z","updated_at":"2025-08-29T17:12:06Z","body":"Thanks for testing! This is actually an unintended consequence -- this mesh can simplify cleanly to 1024 triangles, but the next step can only simplify to 514 triangles due to locked borders - just shy of the goal (512). When pruning is enabled, simplifier is determined to get to the specified number which includes creating a 0-triangle LOD, which makes it so that we terminate the generation process. You can observe that difference by looking at the logs in --verbose mode now.\r\n\r\nSo your code previously was displaying a 514-triangle LOD, and with this change as is, the last LOD was the 1024-triangle LOD that still had a clean tessellation.\r\n\r\nI'm going to take a look at improving this in meshoptimizer in the future because this part of behavior is not super helpful, but for now I adjusted the code to try to get as low as we can with pruning and, if this situation happens, to retry without it. This will probably be unnecessary in the future, but it prevents a possibility of a final low quality LOD to be skipped as a side-effect of this change. That adjustment doesn't normally change the behavior, e.g. the safe mesh from my original description simplifies the same as it did without this tweak.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3235113001/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"perf